Capture log for issue #298 (self-hosted SearXNG chat web search).
All commands run 2026-08-30 from this PR's own worktree, against the
committed deploy/searxng/settings.yml and the searxng service added to
deploy/docker/docker-compose.yml. No credentials, tokens or secrets appear
below; SEARXNG_SECRET used here is the compose dev fallback
"hive-local-searxng-secret", not a production value.

====================================================================
1. Bring the real compose-wired service up (not a hand-typed `docker run`)
====================================================================

$ cd deploy/docker && docker compose --profile local up -d searxng
 Network hive-agent-a7ab50cd50799a3eb-2e1382eb_default  Created
 Volume "hive-agent-a7ab50cd50799a3eb-2e1382eb_searxng-data"  Created
 Container hive-agent-a7ab50cd50799a3eb-2e1382eb-searxng-1  Started

$ docker ps --filter "name=searxng" --format "{{.Names}}\t{{.Status}}"
hive-agent-a7ab50cd50799a3eb-2e1382eb-searxng-1	Up 10 seconds (healthy)

Healthcheck (wget --spider http://127.0.0.1:8080/healthz inside the
container) passed on its own, confirming the committed settings.yml mount,
the SEARXNG_SECRET environment override and the port mapping all wired up
correctly through compose, not just through a manually-typed `docker run`.

====================================================================
2. Real JSON-API query through the compose-wired instance
====================================================================

$ curl -s "http://127.0.0.1:8888/search" --get \
    --data-urlencode "q=hive api gateway" --data-urlencode "format=json" \
    | python3 -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); \
        print('num_results:', len(d.get('results',[]))); \
        print('unresponsive_engines:', d.get('unresponsive_engines'))"

num_results: 10
unresponsive_engines: [['brave', 'too many requests'], ['duckduckgo', 'CAPTCHA'], ['google', 'CAPTCHA']]

This confirms: JSON format is being served at all (`formats: [html, json]` in
settings.yml took effect -- SearXNG 403s a JSON request otherwise), and a
search returns a full page of results even with 3 of 4 configured engines
suspended, because the 4th (bing here) still answered. See the issue #298
comment and the PR body for the full engine-availability discussion.

====================================================================
3. Engine availability across 5 queries, standalone container
   (same image + settings.yml, run before the compose service existed,
   used to characterize behavior under sustained querying)
====================================================================

Query: test
  latency_s: 0.69
  unresponsive_engines: [['brave', 'too many requests'], ['duckduckgo', 'CAPTCHA'], ['google', 'CAPTCHA']]
  num_results: 10
  engines_present_in_results: ['bing']

Query: canadian mortgage rates
  latency_s: 0.31
  unresponsive_engines: [['brave', 'Suspended: too many requests'], ['duckduckgo', 'CAPTCHA'], ['google', 'Suspended: CAPTCHA']]
  num_results: 10
  engines_present_in_results: ['bing']

Query: python asyncio task groups
  latency_s: 0.30
  unresponsive_engines: [['brave', 'Suspended: too many requests'], ['duckduckgo', 'CAPTCHA'], ['google', 'Suspended: CAPTCHA']]
  num_results: 10
  engines_present_in_results: ['bing']

Query: capital of bangladesh
  latency_s: 0.29
  unresponsive_engines: [['brave', 'Suspended: too many requests'], ['duckduckgo', 'CAPTCHA'], ['google', 'Suspended: CAPTCHA']]
  num_results: 10
  engines_present_in_results: ['bing']

Query: latest openai model release
  latency_s: 0.28
  unresponsive_engines: [['brave', 'Suspended: too many requests'], ['duckduckgo', 'CAPTCHA'], ['google', 'Suspended: CAPTCHA']]
  num_results: 9
  engines_present_in_results: ['bing']

A one-off manual curl against a freshly started container, run before this
5-query loop, DID get results attributed to brave, bing AND google together
on a single cold query. The very next request (the "test" query above,
request #2 to that same fresh container) already shows google/duckduckgo/
brave suspended. Read together: this sandbox's egress IP tolerates roughly
one query before Google/DuckDuckGo/Brave's anti-bot systems trip, after which
only Bing keeps answering for the rest of the ~120s max_ban_time_on_fail
window. That is the CAPTCHA risk issue #298 itself named for datacentre IP
ranges. The demo box is on a residential connection, which is the favourable
case per the issue, but that has NOT been verified here -- see the PR body's
outstanding-verification note.

